adjudication.rationale:
In `reauthenticationOfUserWithoutPasskey`, the check is:
```java
try {
  MatcherAssert.assertThat(driver.findElement(...), nullValue());
  fail(...);
} catch (Exception nsee) { /* expected */ }
```
If the element is absent, `findElement` throws `NoSuchElementException` (an `Exception`) and the catch passes. If the element is present, `findElement` returns a non-null `WebElement` and `assertThat(..., nullValue())` throws an `AssertionError` (an `Error`, not an `Exception`), which is *not* caught and will fail the test. So the test does not “unconditionally” pass in both outcomes; it fails when the webauthn element is present. The `fail()` is indeed effectively unreachable, but that doesn’t make the assertion meaningless.
